WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:02.413
MAX SALTONSTALL: Today
we're talking about the ROI

00:00:02.413 --> 00:00:04.980
for Anthos, some price cuts,
and new DataProc features.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.680
I'm Max Saltonstall, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud," where

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.818
we serve you the
lowest-latency news.

00:00:10.818 --> 00:00:12.360
One of the key tenets
of Google Cloud

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.580
is helping our users save
money while empowering

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.838
them to do more.

00:00:15.838 --> 00:00:17.130
But don't take our word for it.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:19.500
Check out Forrester's new
technology projection.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.990
In the total economic
impact of Anthos,

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:23.490
they found key
financial benefits

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.550
across operational efficiency,
developer productivity,

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:29.530
security productivity,
and customer retention.

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:32.440
So read through and reap some
of those benefits yourself.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:35.160
And speaking of budgets, we
just announced price cuts

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.620
for the NVIDIA T4 GPU.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.180
Google Cloud is
committed to making

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.670
GPU acceleration
accessible to all users,

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:43.890
from garages to corporations.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:46.380
With the reduced cost
of NVIDIA T4 instances,

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:48.720
we now have a broad
selection of accelerators

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.720
for a multitude of workloads,
performance levels, and price

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.700
points.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.350
In the land of
DataProc, we've just

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:58.200
graduated several new features
to generally available which

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.620
extend our data science and
machine learning capabilities.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:04.319
Autoscaling and notebooks
can help streamline

00:01:04.319 --> 00:01:07.260
your environment, while
accelerator support for GPUs

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:09.750
saves you some effort when
you're working on deep learning

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:10.640
models.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:13.500
So go deep and let us
know what you think.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.690
And in the world of G Suite,
we've just acquired AppSheet.

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:18.240
AppSheet has been
powering businesses

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:21.330
with its no-code platform,
making it simple for anyone

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:24.690
to leverage Google Sheets,
or Maps, or Cloud Functions,

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:27.450
or whatever their heart dreams
of into an application that

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:30.210
can automate and simplify
the workday for everyone.

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.327
Welcome to the team, y'all.

00:01:32.327 --> 00:01:34.410
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:36.510
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:37.690
Thoughts or ideas?

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:39.400
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.870
We'll see you in the cloud.

